          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: an event was created 145 minutes after Pending Close\n\nThe relevant Racine manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack**. One associated cost event was created after the September cost period entered Pending Close.\n\n| Audit item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | CE-250904-0004 |\n| Event type | INPUT — component issue |\n| Amount | **USD $318,250.75** (31,825,075 cents) |\n| Cost period | Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09 |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T20:25:00** |\n| Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **145 minutes — 2 hours, 25 minutes** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\n**Calculation:** `20:25:00 − 18:00:00 = 8,700 seconds ÷ 60 = 145 minutes.`  \nThe timestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; no time-zone offset was supplied.\n\n### Policy conclusion\n\n**The recorded POSTED status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment**, based on the supplied period state and records.\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* section states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and will be processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close can continue processing. The stated exceptions—revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments—do **not** cover this ordinary component-issue INPUT event.\n\n**Sources:** Supplied `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` records from `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle SCM Cost Management 26B policy excerpt, PDF page **233**, printed page **225**.\n\nNo database records were changed. The audit report was submitted and verified, and the result with provenance was saved to `/cache/work/worker_b6b4b8cc5fe5/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
